---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { interests, papers } from '../../data/site';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const cards = [
 { href:'/research/evomaxx', tag:'Artificial life', cls:'live', title:'EvoMaxx', when:'Apr to Nov 2026', text:'An evolving artificial chemistry on the GPU, with its rule space mapped by controlled experiments and twelve A-life papers reproduced.' },
 { href:'/research/slavemaker', tag:'Agent-based model', cls:'work', title:'Slavemaker Swarm', when:'2026', text:'Polyergus raids on Formica colonies: pheromone recruitment, enslavement, usurpation and host–parasite coevolution.' },
 { href:'/research/aeass', tag:'Paper', cls:'pause', title:'AEASS v3', when:'2025, revised 2026', text:'A memetic algorithm that solves the hardest known 9×9 Sudokus, with an audit of a broken earlier version and a full ablation.' },
 { href:'/research/smart-zebra', tag:'B.Sc. thesis', cls:'', title:'Smart Zebra', when:'2025 to 2026', text:'Teaching a 3B language model logic-grid reasoning with SFT, GRPO and an AC-3 prompt. With Onur Kansoy, equal contribution.' },
];
const repro = [
 { name: 'BEECLUST aggregation with Kilobots', src: 'Bodi, Thenius, Schmickl, Crailsheim (2009)', status: 'Fig. 5 and the aggregation times of Fig. 7 reproduced in ARGoS with simulated Kilobots; the two-swarm experiments are still to do.', href: 'https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/swarm-reproductions/tree/main/01_beeclust' },
 { name: 'Onset of collective motion', src: 'Vicsek et al. (1995)', status: 'Simulation and figures done; the write-up of the critical exponents is pending.', href: 'https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/swarm-reproductions/tree/main/02_vicsek1995' },
 { name: 'NEAT on XOR', src: 'Stanley & Miikkulainen (2002)', status: 'Solved in 100 of 100 runs as in the paper, but with about 35% more evaluations and larger networks.', href: 'https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/swarm-reproductions/tree/main/03_neat2002' },
 { name: 'Gray–Scott patterns', src: 'Pearson (1993)', status: 'Phase diagram and pattern classes reproduced, including the chaos of pattern ε.', href: 'https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/swarm-reproductions/tree/main/04_pearson1993' },
];
const alife = ['Lenia (Chan 2019)', 'Flow-Lenia (Plantec et al. 2023)', 'Physarum transport networks (Jones 2010)', 'Activator–inhibitor (Young 1984)', 'Turing patterns (Gierer & Meinhardt 1972)', 'Cyclic dominance (May & Leonard 1975)', 'Kuramoto synchrony (1975)', 'Random Boolean networks (Kauffman 1969)', 'Edge of chaos (Langton 1990)', 'MAP-Elites (Mouret & Clune 2015)', 'Phyllotaxis (Vogel 1979)', 'Euclidean rhythms (Toussaint 2005)'];
---
<Base title="Research" description="Research of Emre Ertürk in evolutionary computation, artificial life and swarm systems.">
<div class="wrap pagehead"><span class="kicker">Research</span><h1>Local rules, collective behaviour</h1><p class="lead">How do simple, local interactions, between cells, ants or robots, produce structure and adaptive behaviour that none of them was given? I approach this question through evolutionary search, artificial life and agent-based simulation.</p></div>
<div class="wrap section" style="padding-top:10px"><hr class="rule"><div class="rgrid">
 <div class="rv"><h2 class="h2">Interests</h2><ul class="ilist">{interests.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul></div>
 <div class="rv prose"><h2 class="h2">Direction</h2>
  <p>My projects so far are in simulation. EvoMaxx evolves the rules of an artificial chemistry and measures which rule families produce lifelike organisms. Slavemaker Swarm coordinates thousands of agents only through pheromone fields. AEASS asks what an evolutionary algorithm needs in order to work on a tightly constrained problem, and why it had to be memetic.</p>
  <p>The natural next step is to put these ideas on robots: collective behaviour that comes from local sensing, controllers and morphologies found by evolution, and shape that develops from growth rules. That is why I am reproducing swarm robotics papers such as BEECLUST and the Vicsek model, and why I am learning computer graphics, to build the simulators this work needs.</p>
  <!-- TODO(Emre): optional: add a sentence in your own words about the labs or problems you want to work on next. -->
 </div>
</div></div>

<div class="wrap section" style="padding-top:0"><hr class="rule"><h2 class="h2 rv" style="margin-top:26px">Papers and reports</h2>
 <ol class="pubs">{papers.map((p) => <li class="rv"><span set:html={p.authors} />. <a href={`${b}${p.to}`}><b>{p.title}</b></a>. <span class="v">{p.venue}</span>{p.links.length > 0 && <span class="pl">{p.links.map((l) => <a class="mono" href={l.href}>{l.label}</a>)}</span>}</li>)}</ol>
</div>

<div class="wrap section"><h2 class="h2 rv">Projects</h2><div class="wcards">{cards.map(c=><a class="wcard rv" href={`${b}${c.href}/`}><span class={`tag ${c.cls}`}>{c.tag}</span><h3>{c.title}</h3><span class="kicker">{c.when}</span><p>{c.text}</p></a>)}</div></div>

<div class="wrap section" id="reproductions"><hr class="rule"><div class="grid2" style="margin-top:28px">
 <div class="rv"><span class="kicker">Reproductions</span><h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:8px">Swarm and evolutionary computation</h2><div class="prose"><p>Before building on a model, I re-implement it from the paper alone and run the published experiments again. Each reproduction reports what matched, what did not, and why. Faithful baselines matter more than new variants.</p></div>
  <ul class="rlist">{repro.map((r) => <li><a href={r.href}><b>{r.name}</b></a><span class="kicker">{r.src}</span><p>{r.status}</p></li>)}</ul>
  <p style="margin-top:12px"><a class="mono" style="font-size:14px" href="https://github.com/EmreErturk-3/swarm-reproductions">All code and results on GitHub →</a></p></div>
 <div class="rv"><div class="arena"><canvas id="vk" aria-label="Vicsek particles aligning"></canvas></div><div class="met" id="vkh"></div><p class="note">Live Vicsek model: each particle aligns with its neighbours, with noise. The noise sweeps slowly through the ordering transition.</p>
  <figure class="fig" style="margin-top:18px"><img src={`${b}/media/research/beeclust_fig5.webp`} alt="BEECLUST reproduction: fraction of robots aggregated against swarm size" loading="lazy"><figcaption>BEECLUST reproduction, the counterpart of Fig. 5 in Bodi et al. (2009): fraction of Kilobots aggregated in the light against swarm size.</figcaption></figure></div>
</div>
<div class="rv" style="margin-top:36px"><h3 class="sub">A-life models reproduced for EvoMaxx</h3><p class="prose">Twelve more models are reproduced in the EvoMaxx repository, each from its paper, and all of them <a href="/evomaxx/reproductions/live/">run live in the browser</a>:</p><ul class="chips">{alife.map((a) => <li>{a}</li>)}</ul></div>
</div>
</Base>
<style is:global>
.rgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.8fr) minmax(0,1.2fr);gap:44px;margin-top:28px}.ilist{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;font-size:19px}.ilist li{padding-block:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.wcards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}.wcard{background:var(--panel);border:2px solid var(--wall);padding:20px;text-decoration:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;transition:transform .25s,box-shadow .25s;min-width:0}.wcard:hover{transform:translate(-3px,-3px);box-shadow:6px 6px 0 var(--wall);color:inherit}.wcard h3{font-size:27px}
.pubs{margin:0;padding-left:22px;display:grid;gap:16px;max-width:90ch}.pubs li{line-height:1.5}.pubs a{text-decoration:none}.pubs a:hover b{text-decoration:underline}.pubs .v{color:var(--mut);font-style:italic;font-family:var(--serif)}.pubs .pl{display:inline-flex;gap:10px;margin-left:10px;font-size:13px}
.rlist{list-style:none;margin:18px 0 0;padding:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.rlist li{padding-block:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.rlist a{text-decoration:none}.rlist .kicker{display:block}.rlist p{font-size:15.5px;margin-top:4px}
#vk{width:100%;aspect-ratio:1}
.sub{font:500 13px var(--mono);color:var(--mut);margin:0 0 8px;letter-spacing:0}
.chips{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:12px 0 0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}.chips li{font:13px var(--mono);border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel);padding:5px 9px}
@media(max-width:860px){.rgrid,.wcards{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:18px}}
</style>
<script>
import { Vicsek, fit, reduce, metrics } from '../../scripts/sims';
let raf=0;
document.addEventListener('astro:page-load',()=>{const c=document.getElementById('vk') as HTMLCanvasElement;if(!c)return;let f=fit(c);const w=new Vicsek(),h=document.getElementById('vkh')!;new ResizeObserver(()=>{f=fit(c);w.draw(f.g,f.W,f.H)}).observe(c);
const l=()=>{raf=requestAnimationFrame(l);const r=c.getBoundingClientRect();if(r.bottom<0||r.top>innerHeight)return;w.step();w.draw(f.g,f.W,f.H);metrics(h,w.metrics(),true)};if(reduce()){for(let i=0;i<300;i++)w.step();w.draw(f.g,f.W,f.H);metrics(h,w.metrics())}else l()});
document.addEventListener('astro:before-swap',()=>cancelAnimationFrame(raf));
</script>
